<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-AUSTRALIAN P-NOTES - Tenders total A$70 mln.</title>
<headline>RTRS-AUSTRALIAN P-NOTES - Tenders total A$70 mln.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Two promissory note issuers came to the Australian commmercial paper market via tender for a total of A$70 million on Wednesday.</p>
<p>General Property Trust made the larger issue, selling A$40 million of its 90-day p-notes at 6.86 percent or about four basis points over the mid-rate for the corresponding bank bill.</p>
<p>The bank bill yield curve moved up and steepened following inaction on official interest rates from the Reserve Bank of Australia (RBA) this morning.</p>
<p>There had been some speculation of a rate cut today in the lead up to and following Tuesday's RBA board meeting.</p>
<p>&quot;Thirty days are still bid below the cash rate,&quot; a discount securities dealer said. &quot;I think they (yields) will drift up over the next few days.&quot;</p>
